# SSH keys

## Overview

The phone runs an SSH server. `ssh livebook@nerves.local` opens an IEx
prompt on it, and `ssh -s livebook@nerves.local fwup < firmware.fw`
installs a firmware update. It accepts the password (`livebook` unless
the firmware was built with another one) and every public key listed in
this notebook.

The keys live in `/data/nerves_ssh/default_user/authorized_keys`, so
they survive reboots and firmware updates. Flashing a new image erases
them.

**A phone that ever ran firmware v0.2.0 or earlier still accepts the SSH
key of the person who built those images**: the `ED25519` key with
fingerprint `SHA256:7ZM/SmuSfVmHkt69TzXLJ4n9X34aRpORFaEi6yys5Fc`. Delete
it below.

## Helpers

`NervesSSH` keeps the list of authorized keys, one `authorized_keys`
line each, and writes it to `/data` whenever it changes. These helpers
read a line's type, fingerprint and comment, and check a pasted key
before adding it.

```elixir
defmodule SSHKeys do
  def list, do: NervesSSH.configuration().authorized_keys

  def describe(line) do
    case decode(line) do
      [{key, attrs} | _] ->
        %{
          type: line |> String.split() |> hd(),
          fingerprint: to_string(:ssh.hostkey_fingerprint(:sha256, key)),
          comment: to_string(Keyword.get(attrs, :comment, ""))
        }

      _ ->
        %{type: "?", fingerprint: "(unreadable)", comment: ""}
    end
  end

  def add(text) do
    line = String.trim(text)

    cond do
      line == "" ->
        {:error, "Paste a public key first."}

      String.contains?(line, "PRIVATE KEY") ->
        {:error, "That's a private key. Paste the contents of the .pub file instead."}

      String.contains?(line, "\n") ->
        {:error, "Paste one key at a time."}

      decode(line) == [] ->
        {:error, "Not a public key. It should look like: ssh-ed25519 AAAA… you@laptop"}

      line in list() ->
        {:error, "This key is already on the phone."}

      true ->
        NervesSSH.add_authorized_key(line)
    end
  end

  def remove(line), do: NervesSSH.remove_authorized_key(line)

  # :ssh_file.decode/2 raises on malformed key data instead of returning [].
  defp decode(line) do
    :ssh_file.decode(line, :auth_keys)
  rescue
    _ -> []
  end
end
```

## Manage the keys

Delete a key with its button, or paste a public key (the one line in
`~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub` on your computer, for example) and add it. The
list redraws after each change. Deleting every key is fine: the
password still works.

```elixir
defmodule SSHKeys.UI do
  def show do
    frame = Kino.Frame.new()
    render(frame, nil)
    frame
  end

  defp render(frame, message) do
    rows =
      for line <- SSHKeys.list() do
        %{type: type, fingerprint: fp, comment: comment} = SSHKeys.describe(line)
        delete = Kino.Control.button("Delete")

        Kino.listen(delete, fn _event ->
          SSHKeys.remove(line)
          render(frame, "Deleted #{fp}.")
        end)

        Kino.Layout.grid([Kino.Markdown.new("`#{type}` `#{fp}` #{comment}"), delete],
          columns: 2
        )
      end

    rows = if rows == [], do: [Kino.Markdown.new("_No keys: only the password works._")], else: rows

    form =
      Kino.Control.form([key: Kino.Input.textarea("Public key")],
        submit: "Add key",
        reset_on_submit: [:key]
      )

    Kino.listen(form, fn %{data: %{key: text}} ->
      case SSHKeys.add(text) do
        :ok -> render(frame, "Added #{SSHKeys.describe(String.trim(text)).fingerprint}.")
        {:error, reason} -> render(frame, reason)
      end
    end)

    status = if message, do: [Kino.Markdown.new("**#{message}**")], else: []

    Kino.Frame.render(frame, Kino.Layout.grid(status ++ rows ++ [form], columns: 1))
  end
end

SSHKeys.UI.show()
```

## From IEx

The same, over `ssh livebook@nerves.local`:

```elixir
NervesSSH.configuration().authorized_keys
```

```elixir
# NervesSSH.add_authorized_key("ssh-ed25519 AAAA… you@laptop")
# NervesSSH.remove_authorized_key("ssh-ed25519 AAAA… you@laptop")
```
